  "articleBody": "Turning an underused garage into a finished living suite, home office, or rec room sounds straightforward, but cutting corners creates expensive headaches down the road.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\n- Skipping Building Permits: Starting construction without required municipal building permits can stop your remodel cold and complicate property sales later.\n- Fastening Untreated Lumber to Concrete: Placing standard lumber directly against a concrete slab invites rot; pressure-treated base plates or moisture barriers are vital.\n- Overlooking Ceiling Height and Egress: Habitable space rules mandate specific ceiling clearances and compliant emergency exit paths that unfinished garages rarely have initially.\n- Ignoring Slab Moisture: Sealing or covering concrete that wicks groundwater leads to ruined flooring, persistent dampness, and mold behind new drywall.\n- Forgetting Vehicle Parking Rules: Converting your primary garage may trigger municipal planning reviews regarding required off-street parking spots.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nStructural framing changes, fire separation between garage bays and living spaces, and running new plumbing or electrical circuits require licensed trade coordination. \n\nHH Remodeling LLC handles garage conversions, structural framing, drywall, and interior finishes throughout the Denver metro. Call 303-505-0866 to talk through your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
